** Text sync (pure diff + in-place renames)
The map model: region root row holds the MAP title (structural,
never a member); member files map 1:1 to non-root rows in MM_ORDER.
my/mm-sync--diff computes (ADDED REMOVED ROOT-OK SUBS) without
writing anything: exact text matches pair free, leftovers zip in
order, fitting renames become SUBS, no-fit pairs split to
added/removed, root-ok requires exactly one parent-less row whose
text equals the map title. my/mm-sync--apply-text performs SUBS
only on the rename-only path (no structural change, so positions
stay valid). Anything structural goes to the rebuild phase, which
renders all titles fresh. Never throws.
